      "id": "intro-to-operators",
      "title": "Introduction to Operators",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "3m",
      "content": "<p>Operators are special symbols in Python that carry out arithmetic or logical computation. The value that the operator operates on is called the operand.</p>\n<p>For example: <code>x + y</code>, here <code>+</code> is the operator and <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> are operands.</p>"
    },
    {
