    {
      "id": "comparison-operators",
      "title": "Comparison Operators",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "4m",
      "content": "<p>Comparison operators compare the values on either side of them and decide the relation among them. They return a Boolean value: <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>==</code> Equal</li>\n<li><code>!=</code> Not Equal</li>\n<li><code>></code> Greater than</li>\n<li><code><</code> Less than</li>\n</ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "blank-assignment",
      "title": "Fill in the Blank: Exponentiation",
      "type": "blank",
      "duration": "3m",
      "content": {
        "text": "To raise a number to a power in Python, we use the double asterisk operator: 2 ___ 3 evaluates to 8.",
        "answer": "**"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "logical-operators",
      "title": "Logical Operators",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "4m",
      "content": "<p>Logical operators are used to combine conditional statements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>and</code>: Returns True if both statements are true</li>\n<li><code>or</code>: Returns True if one of the statements is true</li>\n<li><code>not</code>: Reverse the result, returns False if result is true</li>\n</ul>"
    },
